text Could it be that...
text When the old man brought Nagisa here as she was on the verge of death...
text Nagisa became connected to this town from that moment on?
text ...As well as Ushio, her child.
text @[Tomoya]
text ...This town.
sound PQ4.aac
text @[Akio]
text Yeah?
text @[Tomoya]
text This town... must find it painful...
sound PQ5.aac
text @[Akio]
text It's people who build the town.
sound PQ6.aac
text @[Akio]
text I don't think pain has anything to do with it.
sound PQ7.aac
text @[Akio]
text It probably just feels like.... oh, things are changing.
sound PQ8.aac
text @[Akio]
text That's how I'd feel, at least.
text So even when people die...
text We need to simply accept it as something that's happened?
text Is our only reaction supposed to be to say, "Ah, everything is always changing..."?
text But we're human beings.
text Living creatures with emotions.
text Who fight with everything they have...
text To keep from being sad, and from losing what's important to them.
