text Winter has come.
text The air feels frozen.
text I open the curtains to look out my window.
text I gasp.
text For a moment... it looked as if everything had been buried in snow.
text That even buildings had disappeared...
text And that all that was visible was the white plain of winter, as far as the eye can see.
text But it was just my imagination.
text It hasn't snowed enough here to accumulate on the ground for years.
text Even if it does snow, it quickly melts, simply turning the ground wet.
text When I look back into my room, all I see is Ushio, sleeping.
text There's nothing else there.
text All I have is Ushio's life and mine.
text Our lives spent struggling against this illness, day after day.
text I've been by her side the entire time.
text I've run through my savings.
text I have no idea what I'll do next.
text What's going to become of us?
