text There's nowhere we can go now.
text I may lose this life in my arms, yet all I can do...
text ...is hold her, as if I'm protecting her from the falling snow...
text ...And cower in the middle of the street...
text What... am I trying to do...?
text What am I... doing here...?
text That field of flowers is so far and out of reach...
text That figure of Ushio, frolicking and playing there is out of grasp...
text I wanted so badly to be there with her this time, playing alongside her...
text She and I...
text ...would have been able to play and get along so much better than we did that summer day...
text Because now... we're father and daughter.
text We're living together.
text But then...
text And yet...
